gpio-mxc: the two field widths and the is_imx8qm local the stable chain left
half-applied.

Taken from
  https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/incr/patch-6.12.80-81.xz
  https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/incr/patch-6.12.114-115.xz

6.12.114-115 widened both_edges and wakeup_pads to unsigned long so the
set_bit()/clear_bit()/assign_bit() conversions it carries are type-correct. The
struct hunk found no context in reMarkable's tree (the field order differs),
while every conversion hunk landed, so the tree calls bitops on u32 fields and
GCC 16 refuses that.

6.12.80-81 added the is_imx8qm local used by mxc_gpio_set_pad_wakeup(); its hunk
also flips one pad_type_map entry this vendor tree already has, so the whole
hunk was rejected while the guard body it belongs to (a separate hunk) landed --
leaving is_imx8qm undeclared.

Only those two fields and that one declaration change below; the vendor code
otherwise stays as published.

--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-mxc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-mxc.c
@@ -66,10 +66,10 @@
 	struct irq_domain *domain;
 	struct gpio_chip gc;
 	struct device *dev;
-	u32 both_edges;
+	unsigned long both_edges;
 	struct mxc_gpio_reg_saved gpio_saved_reg;
 	bool power_off;
-	u32 wakeup_pads;
+	unsigned long wakeup_pads;
 	u32 wakeup_pads_save;
 	bool is_pad_wakeup;
 	u32 pad_type[32];
@@ -577,6 +577,7 @@
 	unsigned long config;
 	bool ret = false;
 	int i, type;
+	bool is_imx8qm = of_device_is_compatible(port->dev->of_node, "fsl,imx8qm-gpio");
 
 	static const u32 pad_type_map[] = {
 		IMX_SCU_WAKEUP_OFF,		/* 0 */
